        "original_id": "5aaa0b92-8a02-5cbc-9c9a-3948d7fb5e91",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Pine, Butea\n- Taxonomy: Pinus, Pinoideae, species classification\n- Organizations: Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew, Missouri Botanical Garden\n\nFacts:\n- Pinus is the sole genus in the subfamily Pinoideae.\n- The Plant List, compiled by the Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew and the Missouri Botanical Garden, accepts 126 pine species names as current and lists 35 unresolved pine species along with many synonyms.\n- Butea is sometimes classified as having only two species, B. monosperma and B. superba, or as including four or five species.",
